  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SWAAMI (South West Asian Aerosol Monsoon Interactions)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research and development activity contributing to the UK&#x2019;s strategy to address key development challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The SWAAMI project aims to combine measurements of the properties of aerosols across northern India and the Bay of Bengal during the
pre-monsoon season in unprecedented detail, with long term measurements from ground-based networks and data from previous
intensive campaigns, in order to challenge model representations of aerosols over India and their effects on the monsoon. This project is set to have impact across a variety of stakeholders such as policymakers (in evidence for potential climate change mitigation factors), operational weather forecasting centres (in precipitation prediction) and the general public in India via outreach activities.</narrative>
  </description>
